WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.040
Hannah: There's a test coverage gap around pagination. Empty pages and repeated cursors aren't covered.

2
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:14.832
Raj: I'm on it with repeated cursor detection. A repeated token must stop pagination safely.

3
00:00:14.832 --> 00:00:21.311
Lukas: An empty page can still have continuation. Don't automatically treat it as completion.

4
00:00:21.311 --> 00:00:28.151
Anika: Just to confirm, the API allows that, right? I'll ask its owner for an example.

5
00:00:28.151 --> 00:00:35.303
Priya: Okay, one action item per missing case. Maybe cancellation can pair with parser cleanup.

6
00:00:35.303 --> 00:00:43.199
Hannah: We can't rule that out without tests. A successful demo doesn't exercise cancellation behavior.

7
00:00:43.199 --> 00:00:49.535
Lukas: I'll check resource ownership during review. Close the response when the user interrupts.

8
00:00:49.535 --> 00:00:56.182
Raj: A new paging framework would take longer. Let's park that and test our current loop.

9
00:00:56.182 --> 00:01:03.166
Anika: I'll log the unresolved contract question separately. That shouldn't hide the known local gaps.

10
00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:10.150
Priya: Agreed, report test evidence at day's end. No claim of complete coverage until then.

